{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107742","id":2605984888,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6bVCx4","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107742","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107742.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107742.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107742","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107742/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107742/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107742/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/2f4c3d411c7b9bdb10c7bc0e746a161ce7b60f26","number":107742,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Android: Address API 35 UI behavior changes","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Follow-up to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106810 (see https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106810#issuecomment-2914543427).\r\n\r\nAndroid 15+ (target SDK 35+) [enforced edge-to-edge](https://developer.android.com/about/versions/15/behavior-changes-15#edge-to-edge) mode for all apps. Most Godot games are immersive by default, so they should be unaffected (system bars auto dismiss), but non-immersive Godot apps and games will now have part of their UI covered by (transparent) system bars.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106810 addressed the issue for the Android editor by opting out of that behavior, however the opt-out request is no longer respected in Android 16 so it wasn't a full solution.\r\nThis PR instead addresses the issue for Godot apps and games (including the Android editor) by updating Godot's layout padding to take into account the system bars and the display cutout.\r\n\r\nIt also add a new `screen/edge_to_edge` export option to allow apps / games to enable edge to edge support.\r\n\r\nIn addition, the PR also fixes an issue on foldable where the embedded window would obscure the main window when launching.\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch in priority.\r\n\r\nRelevant fixes are cherry-picked for stable branches as needed by maintainers.\r\n\r\nTo speed up the contribution process and avoid CI errors, please set up pre-commit hooks locally:\r\nhttps://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/contributing/development/code_style_guidelines.html\r\n-->\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097562,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc1NjI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/plat